From 87460ae846968bffa047521857adc5e8e40689d7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: yihou <yihou@amd.com>
Date: Fri, 31 Jul 2026 11:25:51 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 09/25] sglang DSA: fix two more descriptions the same audit
 turned up

Follow-up to the patch-2a correction, from re-reading every hedged claim in this
directory against the kits rather than against memory. Two were wrong; the rest
checked out and are left alone.

1. draft_cuda_graph_dp_vote.diff's header still said 02's DP host-sync half "has
   never been tested in isolation either way" -- the same error just corrected in
   02's own header, missed because I fixed one file and not its sibling. It now
   says what is actually true: IndexShare-off does not substitute for 2a either,
   because a host-side sync is invisible to the graph/eager decision both
   mechanisms act on.

2. The upstream table called #31683 "an independent, differently-placed
   implementation of the same indexer fix". That is stronger than what was
   verified. Per its diff, #31683 widens dsa_indexer.forward_cuda's guard from
   seq_lens.numel() == 0 to is_idle() or seq_lens.numel() == 0 -- same function,
   related class of defect, DIFFERENT symptom. The kit recorded it as "adjacent
   only"; the table now matches.

Deliberately left as-is after checking: the "no upstream counterpart" note for
dsa_backend already carries its own limitation (gh search matches titles and
bodies, not diff content) and is PR-DIFF-VERIFIED per-diff; the unmeasured v1
collective cost, the unexercised custom-all-reduce path, the un-re-measured 92%
and the conc=64 ceiling on the IndexShare arm are all real coverage limits rather
than understatements of existing evidence.

Headers re-verified by a real --fuzz=0 apply into a pristine tree: 3/3 clean, 9
files modified.

Co-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
